---
title: Buttermilk Pancakes (example)
servings: 4
---
-- Example recipe shipped with Sous. Your own recipes in recipes/ are gitignored.

= Batter =
Whisk @plain flour{200%g}, @sugar{2%tbsp}, @baking powder{2%tsp}, @baking soda{1/2%tsp} and @salt{1/2%tsp} in a #large bowl{}.

In a #jug{}, whisk @buttermilk{400%ml}, @eggs{2} and @melted butter{40%g} until smooth.

Pour the wet mix into the dry and fold gently until just combined; a few lumps are fine. Let the batter rest for ~rest{10%minutes}.

= Cook =
Heat a #non-stick frying pan{} over medium heat and brush with a little @butter{}(for the pan).

Pour in about 60 ml of batter per pancake and cook until bubbles cover the surface and the edges look set, ~{2-3%minutes}.

Flip and cook the other side until golden, about ~{1%minute}. Keep warm in a low oven while you cook the rest.

Serve with @maple syrup{}(to taste).
